Subject: [PATCH] wlserver: associate SPI touchscreens with the internal display

A touchscreen on an SPI bus never gets a connector: the heuristic in
wlserver_touch_associate_connector only knows i2c as internal and usb as
external, and the udev chain of the TB322FC digitizer is
input -> spi -> spi_master -> platform, with no i2c or usb ancestor.
touch->connector stays nullptr, so wlserver_touchdown and
wlserver_touchmotion skip the connector's orientation transform and the
touch lands at the unrotated (portrait) coordinates of a rotated
(landscape) output.

Treat spi like i2c: both are fixed internal buses, so the association
picks the internal connector and the existing orientation handling
applies unchanged. No angle is hardcoded here; the rotation still comes
from the connector gamescope already selected, exactly as it does for
i2c panels. Calibration, DPI, kernel, USB handling and the UI are
untouched.

---
diff --git a/src/wlserver.cpp b/src/wlserver.cpp
--- a/src/wlserver.cpp
+++ b/src/wlserver.cpp
@@ -484,7 +484,7 @@ static void wlserver_touch_associate_connector(struct wlserver_touch *touch)
 	if (touch->connector != nullptr) return;
 
 	// Heuristic to associate a monitor to a touch input device:
-	//  - if a touchscreen's bus is I²C, it can very likely be associated to an internal monitor.
+	//  - if a touchscreen's bus is I²C or SPI, it can very likely be associated to an internal monitor.
 	//  - if its bus is USB, it can be associated to an external monitor.
 	// This isn't perfect, but we can't rely on the physical sizes reported by both devices,
 	// because it's not uncommon for touchscreens to report wildly incorrect sizes.
@@ -495,7 +495,7 @@ static void wlserver_touch_associate_connector(struct wlserver_touch *touch)
 	while (parent) {
 		const char *subsystem = udev_device_get_subsystem(parent);
 		if (subsystem) {
-			if (strcmp( subsystem, "i2c" ) == 0) {
+			if (strcmp( subsystem, "i2c" ) == 0 || strcmp( subsystem, "spi" ) == 0) {
 				connector = GetBackend()->GetConnector(gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_INTERNAL);
 				break;
 			} else if (strcmp( subsystem, "usb" ) == 0) {
